  "tagline": "A copyleft (LGPL) fork of Redis 7.2.4, now limited to security backports.",
  "description": "Redict was forked from the last BSD-licensed Redis (7.2.4) in March 2024 by Drew DeVault and contributors, with new changes under LGPL-3.0-only and no contributor licence agreement so it can never be relicensed by one company. It aimed to be a stable, conservative Redis rather than a feature-driven one, hosted on Codeberg. In practice Valkey absorbed most of the community momentum, and Redict's recent releases (through 7.3.6 in October 2025) are mainly CVE fixes backported from Valkey. It works as a drop-in Redis 7.2, but there is little reason to choose it for new deployments.",
